    "kshb",
    "scmp",
    "rthk"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_reptiles",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "February 2022, San Ysidro port of entry (California-Mexico border): officers found 52 reptiles (43 horned lizards and nine snakes) in small bags hidden in a man's jacket, trouser pockets and clothing; he later pleaded guilty to smuggling and wildlife trafficking. Narration: 'Another man hid 52 reptiles in his clothes.' Label 'SAN YSIDRO BORDER, CALIFORNIA · 2022 / 43 horned lizards, 9 snakes · he pleaded guilty'.",
   "sources": [
    "cbs_sac",
    "kshb",
    "nbc",
    "tws"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_lesson",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "official rule",
   "text": "LESSON CARD (practical, for the viewer): CBP's customs declaration (Form 6059B) asks travellers to declare fruits, vegetables, plants, food, meat, birds, snails and other live animals; failure to declare can bring penalties and seizure; CBP says failing to declare food products can result in fines and penalties of up to 10,000 dollars. Rows 'FOOD, PLANTS OR ANIMALS?', 'TICK YES AND DECLARE IT', 'HIDE IT: FINES UP TO $10K'; credit 'CBP Form 6059B · CBP via CNN'. Narration (save cue): 'Flying home with snacks? Save this.'",
   "sources": [
